      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرَبًّى</span></b>  [<i>Reared, fostered, brought up, fed,</i> or
<i>nourished:</i> see 2. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And] <i>Made</i> [or <i>preserved</i>]
<i>with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبّ</span> [or <i>inspissated juice, &amp;c.</i> (see 2, last
sentence but one)]: you say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَنْجَبِيلٌ مُرَبًّى</span> [<i>Ginger so preserved</i>]; as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرَبَّبٌ</span>: (S, K:) and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرَبَّيَاتٌ</span></b>  signifies <i>Preserves,</i> or <i>confections, made
with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبّ</span>; like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرَبَّبَاتٌ</span>. (S in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رب</span>.)

